BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 576.0 Tm (A squarefree semiprime is the product of two distinct primes. Theorem. Let m >= 2 and let a be an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 563.5 Tm (integer with gcd\(a,m\)=1. Infinitely many squarefree semiprimes N satisfy N = a \(mod m\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 544.0 Tm (Proof. Dirichlet's theorem guarantees infinitely many primes p = a \(mod m\) and infinitely many) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 531.5 Tm (primes q = 1 \(mod m\). Fix one such prime q, and vary p through the infinitely many eligible primes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 519.0 Tm (distinct from q. Every N=pq is the product of two distinct primes, and N = a*1 = a \(mod m\). The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 506.5 Tm (products are distinct because p varies. QED.) Tj ET
