BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 464.0 Tm (OEIS A085245 defines a\(n\) as the least positive integer k such that k*2^n+1 is a semiprime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 451.5 Tm (Corollary. The integer a\(n\) exists for every n >= 1; indeed there are infinitely many eligible k.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 432.0 Tm (Proof. Set m=2^n and a=1 in the preceding theorem. There exist infinitely many squarefree) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 419.5 Tm (semiprimes N with N = 1 \(mod 2^n\). Each yields a positive integer k=\(N-1\)/2^n with k*2^n+1=N.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 407.0 Tm (Different N yield different k, so this set of positive k is infinite and therefore has a least) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 394.5 Tm (element. QED.) Tj ET
